# CLAUDE.local.md — personal overrides (example)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (gitignored) and keep only the lines that apply to your
machine. It loads automatically alongside `CLAUDE.md`, after it, so anything here wins.

Use it for facts that are true only for *your* setup — never for team conventions (those go in
`CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/rules/`) and never for secrets you would mind sitting in a plaintext
file.

## Examples

<!-- Local database differs from the defaults in env.example -->
- My local Postgres runs on port 5433, database `mediajira_dev`, user `me`.
- `DATABASE_URL` for ad-hoc scripts: `postgresql://me@localhost:5433/mediajira_dev`

<!-- The `postgres` MCP server needs MCP_DATABASE_URI. That goes in
     .claude/settings.local.json (also gitignored), NOT here, because .mcp.json
     env expansion reads process/settings env, not CLAUDE.local.md:
       { "env": { "MCP_DATABASE_URI": "postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@host.docker.internal:5432/DB" } }
-->


<!-- Tooling installed somewhere non-standard -->
- `gcloud` SDK is at `~/sdk/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud`, not on PATH.
- Use `docker compose -p mediajira-v2 ...` on this machine (I run several stacks).

<!-- Services I skip locally to save resources -->
- Don't try to start `clamav` / `kafka` locally — I run `... up -d backend frontend redis pgbouncer nginx` only.
- `variations-studio-api` is not checked out here; ignore it.

<!-- Personal workflow preferences -->
- When I ask for tests, run just the affected app (`manage.py test <app>`), not the full suite.
